# Transport & auth

- Official MCP TypeScript SDK + Streamable HTTP to `https://mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp`.
- `Authorization: Bearer <API_TOKEN>` from CredentialService — never long-lived in renderer.

# Code Mode (v1)

- Production actions use **reviewed deterministic `execute` templates** via `McpCloudflareAdapter` / `executeReviewedOperation`.
- No arbitrary JS from user text; no “run arbitrary MCP code” UI.
- `search` for dev/diagnostics only — not on every button click.
- Connection test: MCP `whoami`. Zone list: paginate; never assume ≤20 zones.

# Safe execute (§4.3)

Never concatenate unsanitized zone IDs, domains, DNS values, expressions, or labels into executable JS. Use a shared encoder that serializes dynamic values safely before template interpolation.

# Capabilities & errors

- Capability states: `available`, `unavailable`, `permission_missing`, `plan_restricted`, `unknown`, `loading` — disable UI with reason; do not confuse permission vs plan.
- Normalize errors to app codes (§16): e.g. `AUTH_INVALID`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `PLAN_RESTRICTED`, `MCP_TOOL_ERROR`.
- Every MCP call: explicit timeout/`AbortSignal` (§18). Respect `Retry-After` for bulk/task engine.
